<title>UK: Schering rating raised at Goldman.</title>
<headline>Schering rating raised at Goldman.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Schering AG was raised to &quot;market outperformer&quot; from &quot;market performer&quot; at Goldman Sachs, a research note from analysts Mark Tracey and John Murphy said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Goldman also raised its earnings per share estimates for the German pharmaceutical group by seven percent for the current year and by between two and three percent thereafter.</p>
<p>It said the moves reflected a series of positive factors including Schering's improving business profile, strategic moves enhancing focus and ongoing cost rationalisation.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 5106</p>
